# What the site deploy uploads, which is not what this repository contains.
#
# The Vercel project's Root Directory is `website`, but the CLI uploads the
# directory it is run from, and `vercel` has to run from here for that setting
# to resolve. So the upload is the whole repository unless this file says
# otherwise, and the whole repository is mostly C++ build trees: a deploy
# refused with
#
#     `files` should NOT have more than 15000 items, received 21211
#
# once a local `third_party` existed, which is 15,726 files on its own. The
# build directories beside it are another 2.9GB.
#
# So this ignores everything and names the two things the build reads back.
# `npm run build` is `node scripts/sync-docs.mjs && next build`, and
# sync-docs reads `../docs/*.md` to generate the contributing section; nothing
# else in the site resolves a path outside `website`. Adding a third such
# source means adding it here, and the symptom if you forget is a build that
# cannot find a file it has locally.
/*

!/website
!/docs
